 "answer": "To stop `promptfoo eval` from writing the results into the `promptfoo` directory, you can use the `--no-write` option. This option is specifically designed to prevent the results from being saved to the default directory. According to the context provided in the project's documentation:\n\n- In the \"Command line > `promptfoo eval`\" section, the `--no-write` option is described as: \"Do not write results to promptfoo directory.\"\n\nSo, when you run the `promptfoo eval` command, simply include the `--no-write` option like this:\n\n```bash\npromptfoo eval --no-write\n```\n\nThis will ensure that the evaluation results are not written to the `~/.promptfoo` directory.",
